<title>TURKEY: SAMBA's Turkey branch sold to local company.</title>
<headline>SAMBA's Turkey branch sold to local company.</headline>
<dateline>ANKARA 1997-01-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>SAMBA Turk, the fully-owned subsidiary of the Riyadh-based Saudi American Bank, was sold to a local company for an undisclosed price, SAMBA Turk said in a statement.</p>
<p>It said the buyer, also undisclosed, was owned by Halit Cingillioglu, vice-chairman of the private Demirbank.</p>
<p>The statement said the buyer had applied to the government to change the bank's name to Ulusal Bank Turk.</p>
<p>It gave no other details.</p>
<p>--Ankara Newsroom, 90-312-4462940</p>
